; Batch quote fetching: getquote is invoked once with --batch for all
; commodities rather than once per commodity (issue #588).
;
; This test exercises prefetch_quotes() and commodity_batch_quote_from_script()
; by using a mock getquote script that supports the --batch protocol.  Three
; different stock commodities are held in the journal; the batch script returns
; a price for each in a single invocation, and --market converts them all to $.
;
; The mock answers single-mode requests one dollar higher than batch mode, so
; the balance below holds only if the one batch call priced every stock.  $,
; the commodity the stocks are priced in, is never requested.  AAPL also has
; the alias Apple; the second block reads back the price database the batch
; wrote and shows that AAPL was requested once, not once per name.

commodity AAPL
    alias Apple

2024/01/15 Buy Stock A
    Assets:Brokerage        10 AAPL
    Assets:Checking        $-1000.00

2024/01/15 Buy Stock B
    Assets:Brokerage        20 GOOG
    Assets:Checking        $-2000.00

2024/01/15 Buy Stock C
    Assets:Brokerage        5 MSFT
    Assets:Checking        $-500.00

test bal --market --download --now 2030/06/15 --getquote $sourcepath/test/scripts/mock-batch-getquote.sh -> 0
            $3700.00  Assets
            $7200.00    Brokerage
           $-3500.00    Checking
--------------------
            $3700.00
end test

test -f $FILE bal --market --download --now 2030/06/15 --getquote $sourcepath/test/scripts/mock-batch-getquote.sh --price-db "${PDB:=$(mktemp)}" > /dev/null && LC_ALL=C sort "$PDB" && rm -f "$PDB"
P 2024/06/15 00:00:00 AAPL $150.00
P 2024/06/15 00:00:00 GOOG $180.00
P 2024/06/15 00:00:00 MSFT $420.00
end test
